minee, so no candidate-level evidence exists yet. No general-election polls or expert ratings are available, leaving fundamentals to carry the forecast.\n\nThe clearest in-state signal is Josh Shapiro, who leads his reelection bid by sixteen points, though Pennsylvania voters are split on whether they want him to seek the presidency and he ranks mid-pack among Democrats nationally in early 2028 polling. With the race two years away and the national environment likely to dominate, a slight Republican edge from the state's lean is the starting point, with wide uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.4565, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.5269, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.504, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.475, "margin": -0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.4803, "margin": -0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.5405, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.485, "margin": -0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.4847, "margin": -0.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.4588, "margin": -1.0}]}